            "review_title": "Review at Hương - Craft Beer & Vienamese Flavors",
            "review_text": "Trâmm L\n3 contributions\n1\nA Hidden Vintage Gem in Da Nang! Outstanding Green Rice Craft Beer\nMay 2026 • Friends\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ An absolute must-visit for craft beer lovers!\n\nDuring my trip to Da Nang, I was looking for a local pub that wasn’t too touristy or loud, and Huong Beer was an incredible find. The atmosphere here is brilliant. It is set in a rustic, open-air garden with a beautiful nostalgic Vietnamese vibe—think old textured walls, warm fairy lights, and wooden furniture. It feels like stepping back in time, offering a perfect, laid-back escape from the bustling city streets.\n\nThe absolute highlight of the night was their signature Green Rice Craft Beer. As a European, I’ve tried many beers, but this one was truly unique—light, crisp, and beautifully aromatic with a subtle, nutty sweetness of autumn rice. We paired it with some of their traditional BBQ and local tapas (đồ mồi), which were bursting with authentic flavors and perfectly complemented the cold brews.\n\nThe staff were incredibly welcoming and helpful, making us feel right at home despite the slight language barrier. If you want to experience authentic Da Nang nightlife with great drinks and a cozy vintage atmosphere, do yourself a favor and visit Huong Beer!\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nGreen Rice Craft Beer, smoked goose breast, tre tron Binh Dinh\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten May 18, 2026",
